{"id": "4dbed783-efaa-4bc8-8e04-800a8ac6ab22", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check the runtime's recent metrics and logs, and the Bedrock model invocation metrics, for errors and throttling over the last hour.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_lt91tRd6k4I4S4z9U1sncD", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "agentcore-search-agent-health", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics", "searching-logs", "verifying-with-docs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine whether model calls (Amazon Bedrock InvokeModel/Converse etc.) made by the Bedrock AgentCore runtime 'llmops_eval_search_agent' are currently failing or being throttled.",
  "context": "User asks 'right now', so focus on the most recent window versus a baseline. This is a shallow status check, not a root-cause hunt. AWS account 123456789012 (agent space account), region us-east-1. First locate the runtime (bedrock-agentcore-control list_agent_runtimes / get_agent_runtime) to get its runtime ID/ARN and log group (typically /aws/bedrock-agentcore/runtimes/<runtimeId>-<endpoint>). Then check: (1) CloudWatch metrics in AWS/Bedrock (Invocations, InvocationClientErrors, InvocationServerErrors, InvocationThrottles, InvocationLatency, by ModelId) and in the Bedrock-AgentCore namespace (Invocations, Throttles, SystemErrors, UserErrors, Latency) for the runtime; (2) the runtime's CloudWatch log group for ThrottlingException, ServiceUnavailable, ModelTimeout, ModelErrorException, AccessDenied, ValidationException, 429/5xx messages; (3) any Bedrock service quota hints if throttling is observed (which model, which quota). Also check whether Bedrock model invocation logging exists to attribute calls to this runtime if the metrics cannot be attributed.",
  "resources": ["AgentCore runtime: llmops_eval_search_agent", "region us-east-1", "account 123456789012"],
  "timeframe": "2026-11-25T15:38:10Z/2026-11-25T16:38:10Z (last hour); baseline: previous 24h",
  "criteria": "Report concisely: is it failing/throttled now (yes/no/inconclusive), counts and rates of errors/throttles per model and per 5-min bucket, representative error messages with timestamps, whether the problem is ongoing or has recovered, and any caveat on attribution (Bedrock metrics are per model/account, not per runtime). If the runtime cannot be found or there is no data, say so explicitly. Do not make mutating calls."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Check AgentCore runtime and Bedrock for errors and throttling"}], "created_at": null}

